Article 6 (Establishment of Directly Controlled Institutions)
(1) The Armed Forces Medical School shall be established under the Armed Forces Medical Command to educate military medical personnel and conduct research and development concerning academic and technical aspects of military medicine.
(2) Hospitals, medical research institutes, and other necessary facilities may be established under the Armed Forces Medical Command to take charge of the following matters:
1. Medical treatment for patients of the respective armed services (including family members of military personnel, civilian emergency patients residing near military units, and other patients designated by the Minister of National Defense);
2. Education of medical personnel;
3. Medical supply;
4. Pathological testing;
5. Other matters concerning hygiene.
(3) Matters concerning the organization and allocation of duties of the Armed Forces Medical School under paragraph (1), hospitals and medical research institutes under paragraph (2), and other necessary facilities shall be determined by the Minister of National Defense.
